## 4. Falsifiability of the design itself

The spike is designed so it can fail: thresholds are frozen before the sample is drawn
(`…:257-272`, SM-1), re-freezing after seeing data is an enumerated illegal transition
(`…:273-281`), verdict downgrades are cheap while upgrades require a new in-closure citation
(`…:301-302`), and ties resolve toward `ABSENT` (`…:338-343`). A NO-GO is recorded as a successful
outcome, not a failure (`…:387`).

